# SFT execution status v0.86

2026-09-13. Local fixture-preparation and prepared-launch components are now
implemented and synthetic-tested. Gate 5 remains incomplete. This is progress
within the existing import task, not an additional roadmap gate.

## Completed local components

- Fixed generated-input preparation: 16 tests. Reuses the frozen 736-parameter
  generator and metadata writer, accepts only a fresh empty private directory,
  checks exact generated inventories, and exposes no input checkpoint, model
  configuration or callback argument. No importer runs in this phase.
- Pure controls builder/validator: 25 tests. Creates the nine bound control files
  from fresh tiny metadata, preserving original bytes and every frozen plan
  limit. Already prepared bases cannot be relabelled with a new nonce.
- Private layout installer: 21 tests. Checks the pinned source/entry/helper,
  rebuilt controls and generated input hashes before writes. New destinations
  are exclusive. Only the fresh private extracted copy is normalized/frozen;
  old source/archive/evidence is not changed.
- Prepared launch adapter: 16 tests. Binds the entire private layout and all
  source/entry/control/nonce pins, copies mutable controls, dispatches the
  existing guardian once and requires its full lifecycle/cleanup evidence.

All 78 new tests and 195 prior regression tests pass on Python 3.11.15 and
3.13.7: 273 tests per runtime, no failures, errors or skips. Final test processes
denied network/process/native-library calls and ML imports with audit hooks.
No prohibited operation was attempted and no ML module was loaded. Eight new
Python files pass syntax and 100-column checks; Ruff was not available.

Cross-component tests exercise generation-byte-surrogate to controls, controls
to the frozen prepared entry/resource validator, controls to layout, and the
actual installer-returned layout to the launch validator. Tensor generation,
filesystem/rootfs installation and guardian dispatch are not native results.

Review also fixed two error-code problems in the new generator: consumed
attempts now consistently report already_attempted even after an ML import;
deadlines wrapped by the frozen helper still report deadline_exhausted.
Neither fix changes the old generator or permits a retry.

## What is still required before native qualification

1. Bind the fixed generator to an authenticated unprivileged Linux worker with
   externally enforced containment and deadline. Its callable API is not that
   enforcement or an authorization.
2. Connect generation, controls, installation and the prepared-launch adapter
   to the existing accepted-runtime qualification harness, with a fresh pinned
   source-admission manifest and independent parent supervision.
3. Execute and verify the generated-only Linux qualification. This native run
   has not happened, and these local tests cannot replace it.

After that, the existing dedicated-host/runtime, external-writer exclusion,
full-size resource admission and real checkpoint CPU import remain, followed by
the documented GPU-worker/private-data/CUDA-smoke prerequisites and SFT.

The tiny generator has a 30-second cooperative deadline and a 4 MiB/32-file
final-input ceiling; final-size checking is not cumulative write metering.
The controls preserve the frozen import-write cap and use the prior tiny
8 MiB DCP payload-read reservation. Installer content writes are separately
bounded at 10 MiB. The installer does not read new inputs back; subsequent
native import audits remain mandatory. These figures are not combined caps,
actual host-capacity proof or full-size performance measurements.

No model/tokenizer/dataset payload, native tensor generation, Linux mount or
guardian, network/S3/instance, GPU, inference or training operation occurred.
All new files are local. Prior source/evidence and CI are unchanged; there was
no commit or push. Public real import remains closed at host_guard_not_bound.
Execution permission, training authorization and production eligibility remain
false. No GPU is needed for the remaining harness-integration code.

